 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Same subject or a different subject",
     "texto": [
      "When **you** want to do something, the verb goes in the **infinitive**: **quiero venir**.\n\nWhen you want **someone else** to do something, you use **que** and the **present subjunctive**: **quiero que vengas**.\n\n- Same subject → **infinitive**: espero llegar pronto.\n- Different subject → **que + subjunctive**: espero que llegues pronto.\n\nThe subjunctive comes from the **yo** form of the present, changing the vowel: **-ar → e** (hablo → **hable**) and **-er / -ir → a** (como → **coma**, vivo → **viva**)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "The regular present subjunctive",
     "texto": [
      "These are the three model verbs, with all six persons:\n\n- **hablar** → hable, hables, hable, hablemos, habléis, hablen\n- **comer** → coma, comas, coma, comamos, comáis, coman\n- **vivir** → viva, vivas, viva, vivamos, viváis, vivan\n\nThe rule is simple: **-ar** verbs use **e** and **-er / -ir** verbs use **a**. Start from the **yo** form: if «yo» is irregular, the subjunctive is too: vengo → **vengas**.\n\nRemember: the person who wants and the person who acts are **different**, and the wish verb comes before **que**."
     ],
